WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:10.780
Recover a dismissed device approval prompt, diagnose a machine showing offline, and choose between SpecWithCode Connect and optional Tailscale fallback routes.

00:11.300 --> 00:25.620
If you clicked Later on a join code prompt, the dialog stays quiet for that unchanged request. Open Settings and Machines and click Show code to reopen or issue a fresh six-character code valid for thirty minutes.

00:26.300 --> 00:40.140
When a computer shows offline, run specwithcode service status and specwithcode connect status on that host. Confirm the service is running, sign out and back in if expired, and update both machines.

00:40.800 --> 00:54.640
SpecWithCode Connect is the default route across Wi-Fi, office networks, and cellular. Use Tailscale or private QR pairing only when you want a direct private network route, and keep MCP for external tools.

00:55.300 --> 01:02.100
All current Connect setup, permission, and recovery guides stay updated in one place on the tutorials hub.
